      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, and here are three archetypes to add immediate friction to your detective's logic: a cynical gang hustler who operates entirely on twisted mercy rather than code, a supernatural cartel enforcer immune to conventional laws who only follows a darker, superstitial logic, and a weary homicide reporter who will sell the truth to save a life but might cross the line first. These three will force your lead to confront the humanity behind the crime, challenging his intellect with raw, messy realities he can't solve with equations alone. Adjust their specific actions and dialogue to barbed wit at every turn, making sure they represent the grit that your polished world lacks.",
